 "actualPublicStdoutEventId": "eb9a1b93-cdbf-4796-a69e-d65d230286d0",
 "actualReturnedReportText": "# RU045 independent whole-batch review\n\n## Snapshot\n- RU: C:\\Users\\stop-\\learning-japanese-ru, branch full-ru-045-body-health-safety, HEAD 9cc3b0a89aa0b7e5de199b863d87fa2d3f97e989.\n- Baseline: 5fd7fe26cd21d2bda4958a0cec2fc828d31bb57e; semantic freeze: bc6881f29d92a7cee8fae069e164492210b118bd.\n- Frozen EN: C:\\Users\\stop-\\.copilot\\session-state\\68a44f7f-62db-4755-8296-fd586c861a35\\files\\ru-full-scope-en-6af98cb, HEAD 6af98cb717755690a9ca793e5454a96ebd7a8f9f.\n- Both HEADs reconfirmed at completion. RU tracked tree clean; pre-existing untracked C:\\Users\\stop-\\learning-japanese-ru\\tools\\__pycache__\\ preserved.\n\n## Actual reading\n- pairs[0:46): all 46 complete EN/RU pairs, 92 bodies: 13 new words and all 33 assigned baseline support pairs. All 648 new Russian lines read. No additional full cards read.\n- objects[0:129): all 129 complete official JMdict objects, including forms, readings, senses and restrictions; entity-expanded serialized XML, not original gzip slices.\n- pool[0:844): all 844 displayed Russian captions compared against the additions, including secondary/different-reading meanings and Russian polysemy. This is NOT 844 full-card reviews.\n- russian[0:1): complete attributed Ожегов–Шведова entry зелёный, all five senses and fixed expressions. The private copyrighted body is not reproduced here.\n- All active guides read: guide0–4, respectively 382/253/138/107/110 lines; all three actual rubrics, 54/43/44 lines. Frozen normative reading: wordformat[125:176), levels[201:275), confusable[0:356).\n- proposals[0:20), invariants[0:1), checks[0:4), selected provenance/dependency/link fields and exact instruction/manifest diffs read. Failed byte-cap requests were split; only successful complete returns count. Assigned unread scope: none. Guidance-inventory hashes were not treated as semantic approval of unread EN documents.\n\n## Separate verdicts\n- **C1 Japanese correctness: CLEAN within the assigned new content.** No confirmed consequential error in preserved examples, readings, forms, sense restrictions or the Russian adaptations. The corrected 生きる citation is 1378520 in the current bytes. Death/result-state, physician/title, suction/drinking, height/noun and weather/illness distinctions remain intact.\n- **C2 adopted coverage/dependencies: CLEAN; overall semantic quiz suitability: UNVERIFIED beyond the qualified protections below.** All 13 additions are complete; no source negative-edge dependency is omitted. Optional navigation does not require recursive authoring, and no absent frozen-target card for 邪 is required. Candidate totals are 1156 runtime units, 844 words and 643 N5 words; manifest version 820f471d66840ea7. The 1143 baseline runtime RAWs and protected tracking/history remain unchanged.\n- **C3 Russian comprehensibility: CLEAN for the 13 new bodies.** No consequential ambiguity, English dependency or misleading Russian explanation found. This is not native-speaker certification or approval of every baseline body.\n\n## Individual assessment of all 20 proposed guards\nI support each only as a conservative direct quiz-label protection, not unrestricted synonymy. This review does not itself advance acceptance. Modern frequency/everyday necessity remains UNVERIFIED for all 20.\n\n1. 体–気分: supported in the qualified physical-health/state reading of самочувствие, not настроение; JMdict 1409140:4, 1222590:1 and the full physical-state explanations.\n2. 体–現実: supported by the distinct たい noun/suffix reality sense, 1409150:3 versus 1263710:1; no change to the からだ lesson.\n3. 医者–先生: supported for respectful reference to a physician, 1159980:1 and 1387990:2; occupation and title are not freely interchangeable.\n4. 危ない–大変: supported for critical/grave conditions and the actual серьёзный label, 1218380:2 and 1415000:3; not all difficult tasks.\n5. 危ない–重い: independently supported for critical/severe illness; the actual label is тяжёлый, grounded by 1335750:5 and the full baseline example, not inferred through 大変.\n6. 吸う–飲む: supported by explicit sipping/slurping, 1228260:2 and 1169870:1; general drinking does not necessarily involve suction.\n7. 死ぬ–止まる: supported by nonliteral cessation, 1310730:3 and 1310620:2; not an equation of death with every stop.\n8. 背–後ろ: supported by rear-side meaning, 2147990:2 and 1269410:1; せい remains separately height-only.\n9. 若い–青い: supported by immaturity/inexperience, 1324300:2 and spelling-restricted 1381390:4, with independently read Russian зелёный sense 5; not an English-only color analogy.\n10. 若い–小さい: supported by explicit young/juvenile meaning 1347750:5 and the small-number sense 1324300:3; not every small adult.\n11. 若い–小さな: independently supported for attributive small numerical value, 1324300:3 and 2136180:1; prenominal grammar preserved.\n12. 若い–低い: independently supported for low numerical value/rank, 1324300:3 and 1434180:1; not low quantity or short stature.\n13. 頭–毛: supported by hair-on-head sense 1582310:2 and 1533820:1; not all fur.\n14. 頭–最初: supported by beginning/start, 1582310:6 and 1293990:1.\n15. 頭–人: supported by the あたま person/head-count sense, 1582310:7 and 1580640:1; no invented free counter construction.\n16. 頭–人間: independently supported by that counted-person sense and actual человек, 1366770:1; not a transitive inference through 人.\n17. 頭–人物: independently supported by that person sense and actual человек within the full label, 1369070:1; not all character/personality meanings.\n18. 頭–主人: supported in the qualified head/person-in-charge/master intersection, 1582310:4 and 1579780:1,3; not every boss, owner or husband.\n19. 風邪–風: supported by the explicitly irregular disease spelling, 1499720:3 and 1583720:1; not merely shared kana.\n20. 風邪–病気: supported for the broad болезнь label within the explicit minor-ailment tendency, 1490230:1 and both complete baseline explanations; not universal medical equivalence.\n\n## Findings and limits\nNo significant issues found in the reviewed changes.\n\nResidual quiz claims remain explicitly UNVERIFIED: 死ぬ–終わる with actual заканчиваться; заканчивать, and 頭–精神/心 with actual психика; дух / сердце; душа. The supplied evidence does not settle those Russian-caption fits. Neither universal safety nor a mandatory additional exclusion is established. No transitive/body/people/negative-adjective clique is endorsed; kana alone does not justify 鼻–花.\n\nThe three-line stdout clarification at C:\\Users\\stop-\\learning-japanese-ru\\.github\\copilot-instructions.md:322–324 has no consequential defect: it provides an additional public return while keeping report-payload, transcript, stdout-wrapper and wire hash domains distinct.\n\nThe four successful validation records are AUTHOR-run evidence, not my executions. I ran no tests, builds or validators, wrote no files, changed no Git state, and contacted/spawned no agents. No live app or ordinary English checkout was accessed. The life/occupation/safety mapping issue remains an app FOLLOW-UP; live status is UNVERIFIED.\n\nAccepted coverage is not advanced: 1143 runtime / 831 words / 630 N5; strict 8278 = 1143 reviewed-current + 2 excluded blocked-media + 7133 pending. C6/C7, media, physical phone, Japanese IME, default activation and release remain separate gates, not new authoring stops. No audio/media, whole-corpus, native or learning-effectiveness certification is given.",
